WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:03.335
-Welcome to "The Tonight Show."
Let's get to some news.

00:00:03.335 --> 00:00:04.804
Well, guys, everybody is talking
about this.

00:00:04.804 --> 00:00:08.507
Yesterday, President Trump did
an interview on Fox News

00:00:08.507 --> 00:00:12.345
where he again tried to defend
his own mental fitness

00:00:12.345 --> 00:00:14.714
by explaining
the cognitive test that he took.

00:00:14.714 --> 00:00:15.982
Watch this.

00:00:15.982 --> 00:00:18.984 line:0%
-It was 30 or 35 questions.
Like, a memory question.

00:00:18.984 --> 00:00:24.757 line:0%
It's -- Like, you'll go,
"Person, woman, man,

00:00:24.757 --> 00:00:28.094 line:0%
camera, TV."

00:00:28.094 --> 00:00:29.795 line:0%
So, they'll say,
"Could you repeat that?"

00:00:29.795 --> 00:00:34.400 line:0%
So it's "person, woman, man,
camera, TV."

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:36.502 line:0%
If you get it in order,
you get extra points.

00:00:36.502 --> 00:00:39.071 line:0%
Okay, now he's asking you
other questions.

00:00:39.071 --> 00:00:40.206 line:0%
"Give us that again."

00:00:40.206 --> 00:00:44.377 line:0%
You go, "Person, woman, man,
camera, TV."

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:46.579 line:0%
It's actually not that easy,
but for me, it was easy.

00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:53.920
[ Laughter ]

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:55.021
-We could have shown you more,

00:00:55.021 --> 00:00:57.924
but our show is only an hour.

00:00:57.924 --> 00:00:58.991
What is he doing?

00:00:58.991 --> 00:01:00.292
He sounds like someone
playing charades

00:01:00.292 --> 00:01:01.794
after pounding Chardonnay.

00:01:01.794 --> 00:01:07.467
He's like, "Man, camera, woman.
Is it a book? Is it a movie?"

00:01:07.467 --> 00:01:09.169
You know, I actually feel
a lot better knowing

00:01:09.169 --> 00:01:10.503
that the President of
the United States

00:01:10.503 --> 00:01:15.041
passed concussion protocol.

00:01:15.041 --> 00:01:16.575
It was impressive until
they asked Trump

00:01:16.575 --> 00:01:18.411
what he ate for lunch that
day, and he said,

00:01:18.411 --> 00:01:25.752
"Person, woman, man,
camera, TV."

00:01:25.752 --> 00:01:28.321
I wish we could see Trump's
answers to the questions

00:01:28.321 --> 00:01:31.257
in written portion, because
I know it looks like this.

00:01:31.257 --> 00:01:34.226
Yeah, that's it.

00:01:34.226 --> 00:01:38.897
The only five names Trump
couldn't remember were his kids.

00:01:38.897 --> 00:01:43.736
[ As Trump ] I want to say
Harry, Zayn, Niall,

00:01:43.736 --> 00:01:45.637
camera, TV.

00:01:45.637 --> 00:01:47.106
[ Normal voice ] He was being
interviewed by one of

00:01:47.106 --> 00:01:50.576
Fox News' top medical
contributors, Dr. Marc Siegel.

00:01:50.576 --> 00:01:53.579
Can we see his face
when Trump was talking?

00:01:53.579 --> 00:01:57.784
You can tell he's thinking,
"Is he having a stroke or am I?"

00:01:57.784 --> 00:02:00.720
Yeah, Trump really seemed
obsessed with those five words,

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:02.822
but it makes sense,
'cause it actually turns out

00:02:02.822 --> 00:02:04.657
he spent a lot of time
studying for the test.

00:02:04.657 --> 00:02:05.925
Check this out.

00:02:05.925 --> 00:02:07.460
-Can you help us?

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:09.562 line:0%
-Yeah.
-Can you say...

00:02:09.562 --> 00:02:15.334 line:0%
-Person, woman, man, camera, TV?

00:02:15.334 --> 00:02:19.972 line:0%
So it's person, woman, man,
camera, TV.

00:02:19.972 --> 00:02:21.107 line:0%
-Hooray!

00:02:21.107 --> 00:02:25.511 line:0%
-Person, woman, man, camera, TV.

00:02:25.511 --> 00:02:26.713 line:0%
-Again!

00:02:26.713 --> 00:02:32.451 line:0%
-Person, woman, man, camera, TV.

00:02:32.451 --> 00:02:34.053 line:0%
-One more time!

00:02:34.053 --> 00:02:40.259 line:0%
-Person, woman, man, camera, TV.

00:02:40.259 --> 00:02:42.361
♪♪
-We did it! We did it!

00:02:42.361 --> 00:02:44.797
-We did it!
-Yay!

00:02:44.797 --> 00:02:47.967 line:0%
-Because I'm cognitively there.

00:02:47.967 --> 00:02:50.236
[ Laughter ]

00:02:50.236 --> 00:02:52.071
-We did it!

00:02:52.071 --> 00:02:53.606
♪♪

00:02:53.606 --> 00:02:55.074
-We did it!

00:02:55.074 --> 00:02:56.875
Listen to this.

00:02:56.875 --> 00:02:59.178
Earlier today,
Joe Biden released a video

00:02:59.178 --> 00:03:01.681
where he sat down with
former president Obama.

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:04.217
They talked about a range of
issues, like healthcare,

00:03:04.217 --> 00:03:07.019
the economy, and, of course,
the COVID pandemic.

00:03:07.019 --> 00:03:08.787
You can tell they're taking
COVID seriously

00:03:08.787 --> 00:03:11.690
because of how far apart they
sat for the interview.

00:03:11.690 --> 00:03:14.827
This is real. Take a look.

00:03:14.827 --> 00:03:17.863
Wow! Wow!

00:03:17.863 --> 00:03:20.466
Obama hasn't distanced himself
from Biden like that

00:03:20.466 --> 00:03:24.837
since the first
10 Democratic debates.

00:03:24.837 --> 00:03:26.306
Usually, in a meeting
that far apart,

00:03:26.306 --> 00:03:27.673
one person's stroking a cat

00:03:27.673 --> 00:03:31.010
while the other's being
lowered into a barracuda tank.

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:35.114
[ As Blofeld ] It's the last
time you mess with me, Mr. Bond.

00:03:35.114 --> 00:03:36.515
[ Normal voice ] Let's get to
some sports news.

00:03:36.515 --> 00:03:38.551
Earlier tonight,
Major League Baseball

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:40.886
made its official return,
and it's clear

00:03:40.886 --> 00:03:43.222
this season's gonna look
pretty different.

00:03:43.222 --> 00:03:46.058 line:0%
-Stadium seats will be empty,
replaced, in some cities,

00:03:46.058 --> 00:03:47.626 line:0%
by cardboard cutouts.

00:03:47.626 --> 00:03:49.629 line:0%
Celebrations will be distanced.

00:03:49.629 --> 00:03:50.997 line:0%
Coaches will be masked.

00:03:50.997 --> 00:03:55.134
-Yeah. Baseball is back,
or, as the president put it,

00:03:55.134 --> 00:04:01.240
"Bat, glove, ball, hot dog, TV."

00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:02.975
Fans have to stay home,
but if you want to feel

00:04:02.975 --> 00:04:05.711
like you're really there,
spend 40 bucks on popcorn

00:04:05.711 --> 00:04:09.148
and then have your kid
spill half of it on the floor.

00:04:09.148 --> 00:04:11.417
That's right -- the NBA has
sealed everyone in a bubble

00:04:11.417 --> 00:04:13.152
in one location,
while Major League Baseball

00:04:13.152 --> 00:04:17.724
is just like, "Let's see how
this goes, baby!"

00:04:17.724 --> 00:04:18.857
Oh, this is interesting, though.

00:04:18.857 --> 00:04:21.560
Fox announced that
they're going to show

00:04:21.560 --> 00:04:24.530
CGI fans in the stands.

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:27.000
Yeah. It will be weird
when a pitcher gets heckled

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:28.534
by the cast of "Toy Story."

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:32.037
[ Light laughter ]

00:04:32.037 --> 00:04:33.773
I don't -- I don't...

00:04:33.773 --> 00:04:36.942
-Yeah, let it go. Let it go.
-Do it!

00:04:36.942 --> 00:04:39.778
Let it go.
-Do it!

00:04:39.778 --> 00:04:41.180
-Alright, well -- Alright.

00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:42.348
[ As Cliff Clavin ] Hey, uh --

00:04:42.348 --> 00:04:44.317
Hey, I think that's
a strike there, uh...

00:04:44.317 --> 00:04:46.352
[ Laughter ]

00:04:46.352 --> 00:04:48.420
-Come on, man.

00:04:48.420 --> 00:04:51.524
[ Normal voice ] Oh.

00:04:51.524 --> 00:04:54.193
Dust off the old Cliff Clavin
impersonation.

00:04:54.193 --> 00:04:55.494
-Just do it.

00:04:55.494 --> 00:04:58.497
There was also some
big football news today.

00:04:58.497 --> 00:05:00.633
While trying to figure out
a permanent name,

00:05:00.633 --> 00:05:02.435
Washington's NFL team
just announced

00:05:02.435 --> 00:05:03.802
a temporary one for this season.

00:05:03.802 --> 00:05:04.904
Listen to this.

00:05:04.904 --> 00:05:06.072 line:0%
-This just in.

00:05:06.072 --> 00:05:08.207 line:0%
Basically, Washington
is going to go with

00:05:08.207 --> 00:05:11.110 line:0%
an interim name
during the 2020 season.

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:15.414 line:0%
It will call itself
the Washington Football Team.

00:05:15.414 --> 00:05:19.585
[ Laughter ]

00:05:19.585 --> 00:05:22.387
What?

00:05:22.387 --> 00:05:24.823
-That's what they came up with?

00:05:24.823 --> 00:05:26.659
That name sounds like
someone tried to talk about

00:05:26.659 --> 00:05:28.260
sports who knows nothing
about sports.

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:33.499
It's like, "I love the
W-Washington Football Team.

00:05:33.499 --> 00:05:39.237
Of course, the I love the
New York Hockey Club Team, too."

00:05:39.237 --> 00:05:45.544
What's a good name?
The Washington Cherry Blossoms.

00:05:45.544 --> 00:05:47.813
Maybe it is hard. I don't know.

00:05:47.813 --> 00:05:50.749
-Oh, how about the -- Is there
a team the Capitals,

00:05:50.749 --> 00:05:51.917
the Washington Capitals?

00:05:51.917 --> 00:05:53.052
-Yeah, there is a team.

00:05:53.052 --> 00:05:54.386
Yeah, it's a great team.

00:05:54.386 --> 00:05:55.988
-Yeah, that's -- Yeah, great.
That's what I thought.

00:05:55.988 --> 00:05:58.190
-Washington Capitals 2.

00:05:58.190 --> 00:06:01.394
-Or Washington Capitals
Part Deux.

00:06:01.394 --> 00:06:03.862
-Deux. Yeah, yeah, exactly.

00:06:03.862 --> 00:06:05.897
Finally, you guys,
you have to see this.

00:06:05.897 --> 00:06:07.600
Yesterday, there was a crazy
storm here in New York,

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:09.634
and someone captured
a pretty amazing moment

00:06:09.634 --> 00:06:10.736
at the Statue of Liberty.

00:06:10.736 --> 00:06:12.705
Look at this thing.

00:06:12.705 --> 00:06:14.207
Whoa.

00:06:18.176 --> 00:06:21.047
Okay, worst case, this damaged
the Statue of Liberty.

00:06:21.047 --> 00:06:25.251
Best case,
we "Freaky Friday" with Canada.

00:06:25.251 --> 00:06:27.353
I'm actually a little worried,
'cause ever since that happened,

00:06:27.353 --> 00:06:29.488
the only thing the Statue of
Liberty can say is,

00:06:29.488 --> 00:06:31.724
"Person, woman, man..."

